# Failures

<!--
  This is this repository's FAILURE TAXONOMY: one entry per kind of failure
  you have seen recur across agent sessions, each naming the recurrence
  signatures it covers. kh-harness scaffolded the shape and will never
  write a failure kind here — naming what went wrong, and deciding whether
  it is a defect in the harness or a limit of the model, is yours. No rule
  is drafted from a recurrence until a failure kind here names it.

  A recurrence is the same tool, the same normalised input and the same
  first error line in two or more sessions under one harness and model.
  `log report` lists them, each with its signature: 16 lowercase hex
  characters, and shows which ones no failure kind below names yet.

  FORMAT — one level-2 heading per failure kind, then one bullet listing the
  signatures it covers, comma-separated:

    ## F<n> — <what kind of failure this is, in a few words>
    - signatures: <signature>, <signature>, ...

  `F<n>` is the letter F and a number, stable, never reused. A heading with
  no signatures line is a failure kind that covers nothing yet. Anything in
  the list that is not a signature, and any level-2 heading not of this
  form, is ignored, and `detect` says how many.

  WORKED EXAMPLE (inside this comment, so it is never read as a failure
  kind — write your own below the comment rather than uncommenting this one):

    ## F1 — The test runner is invoked with a flag this version dropped
    - signatures: 3f9a0c2e7b14d856, a07e5b19c3d2f480
